colemak backspace repeat (keycode 66): stock Colemak remaps <CAPS> to
BackSpace but leaves it non-repeating, and any live xset patch (~/.xprofile,
autostart script) gets wiped whenever mutter/gsd recompiles the keymap
(login, resume from sleep, keyboard hotplug). Real fix: bake repeat=Yes into
the keymap itself via a local XKB override, no root needed. Symbols file at
~/dotfiles/xkb/symbols/custom-repeat, symlinked to
~/.config/xkb/symbols/custom-repeat by install.sh's xkb_stuff(), and enabled
via `gsettings ... xkb-options` including
'custom-repeat(caps_backspace_repeat)'. Survives resume/login because it's
part of what gets recompiled, not a patch applied after the fact. Rerun
`~/dotfiles/install.sh` to (re)apply on a new machine.
